-- A default taken at the root of a section GIVEN is not marked by `l4 nlg`:
-- the call is printed without `surcharge`, so there is no argument for the
-- words "by default" to follow. The decision service's `presumed` list is the
-- account of this default. The second call writes the value, and it prints.

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN surcharge IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`tax on` amount MEANS
    amount PLUS surcharge

#ASSERT (`tax on` WITH amount IS 10) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT (`tax on` WITH amount IS 10, surcharge IS 7) EQUALS 17
